.TH OPSH 1 "2026-10-22" "OpenSH 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opsh \- talk to your terminal in plain English
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opsh
[\fB\-c\fR \fIrequest\fR...] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-e\fR] [\fB\-y\fR] [\fB\-\-copy\fR]
[\fB\-\-shell\fR \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIpowershell\fR]
[\fB\-\-provider\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-model\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-history\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opsh
turns a plain-English request into one command for your shell (PowerShell, bash or zsh) using a
language model, prints it, and runs it. Ordinary shell input such as \fBls\fR or \fBgit status\fR
is recognised locally and runs without calling the model.
.PP
Before a generated command runs, a safety guard checks it against rules for recursive deletes,
disk formatting, raw disk writes, permission changes on system folders, fork bombs, forced process
kills, shutdown and reboot, git history rewrites, piping downloads into a shell, registry and
security changes, and database or infrastructure deletion. Flagged commands are printed with the
reason and only run after an explicit \fBy\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fIrequest\fR...
Handle one request and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print generated commands but never run them.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-explain
Explain each generated command (and why the guard flagged it) and ask before running it.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Run flagged commands without asking. Use with care.
.TP
.B \-\-copy
Copy each generated command to the clipboard (clip, pbcopy, wl\-copy, xclip or xsel).
.TP
.B \-\-shell \fIbash\fR|\fIzsh\fR|\fIpowershell\fR
Shell to generate commands for. Default: \fBOPENSH_SHELL\fR, then \fB$SHELL\fR, then the OS default.
.TP
.B \-\-provider \fIname\fR
Provider for this session: groq, gemini, openai, ollama or mock.
.TP
.B \-\-model \fIname\fR
Model for this session.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-history
Do not read or write the history file.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B !explain\fR, \fB!dry\-run
Toggle explain-before-run or dry run.
.TP
.B !copy
Copy the last generated command.
.TP
.B !history
Show recent input.
.TP
.B !auth
Choose a provider and enter a key.
.TP
.B !\fIcommand\fR
Run \fIcommand\fR as typed, without the model.
.TP
.B !version\fR, \fB!help\fR, \fB!credits\fR, \fB!uninstall\fR, \fBexit
Info, removal and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.opsh/config.json
Provider settings: \fBprovider\fR, and optionally \fBmodel\fR, \fBbase_url\fR, \fBapi_key_env\fR,
\fBtimeout\fR, \fBretries\fR, \fBhistory\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.opsh/.env
API keys (\fBGROQ_API_KEY\fR, \fBGEMINI_API_KEY\fR, \fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fR). Created with mode 600.
.TP
.I ~/.opsh/history
Input history, at most 1000 lines. Lines that look like keys or passwords are not saved.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENSH_PROVIDER\fR, \fBOPENSH_MODEL\fR, \fBOPENSH_BASE_URL\fR, \fBOPENSH_TIMEOUT
Override the provider settings for one run.
.TP
.B OPENSH_SHELL
Shell to generate commands for.
.TP
.B OPENSH_HISTORY
Path of the history file.
.TP
.B OPENSH_MOCK_RESPONSE
With the mock provider, the command to return for every request.
.TP
.B OPENSH_NO_UPDATE_CHECK
Skip the release check at start-up.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Ollama address (default http://localhost:11434).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
opsh \-c "show my public ip address"
opsh \-n \-c "delete all .tmp files"
opsh \-e \-c "free up disk space"
opsh \-\-provider ollama \-\-model llama3.2
OPENSH_PROVIDER=mock opsh \-n \-c "list files"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/muhib-karim/OpenSH
